# Float#abs

abs() -> Float

Get absolute value

```ruby
d = (a - b).abs
```

# Float#+

+(Integer | Float other) -> Float

Perform addition

```ruby
x + 1.0
```

# Float#===

===(untyped other) -> bool

Equality as `case` uses it

```ruby
case x
when 1.0 then hit
end
```

# Float#<=>

<=>(Integer | Float other) -> (Integer | nil)

Compare. Returns -1, 0 or 1

```ruby
a <=> b
```

# Float#/

/(Integer | Float other) -> Float

Perform division

Dividing by 0.0 does not raise; it gives Infinity.
```ruby
x / 2.0
```

# Float#==

==(untyped other) -> bool

Perform equality comparison

**Do not compare floats with ==**; rounding drifts. Compare the size of
the difference.
```ruby
(a - b).abs < 0.001
```

# Float#>=

