# FmrbAudio#load_fmsq

load_fmsq(Integer slot_id, String binary_data) -> void

Put song data into a slot

Loads a tune into a slot. **play_slot is what sounds it.**
```ruby
data = File.open(path, "r") { |f| f.read }
@audio.load_fmsq(0, data)
```

# FmrbAudio#load_fmsq_file

load_fmsq_file(Integer slot_id, String path) -> void

Read a song file into a slot

```ruby
@audio.load_fmsq_file(0,
  "/usr/share/music/round.mml")
```

# FmrbAudio#main_volume=

main_volume=(Integer percent) -> void

Set the volume of the music (MAIN) only

0 to 100 (%), 100 to start with. Only the music of play and of
play_slot on MAIN changes; the effects (SUB), WAVs and the machine's
volume stay. It goes back to 100 when the app closes.
```ruby
@audio.main_volume = 30
```

# FmrbAudio.new

new(FmrbApp app) -> FmrbAudio

Make the sound handler

```ruby
@audio = FmrbAudio.new(self)
```

# FmrbAudio#note_off

note_off(Integer channel) -> void

Stop a note

```ruby
@audio.note_off(0)
```

# FmrbAudio#note_on

note_on(Integer channel, Integer freq) -> void

Sound one note

The frequency is in Hz. It sounds over a tune that is already playing.
```ruby
@audio.note_on(0, 440)
```

# FmrbAudio#pause

pause() -> void

Pause the song

```ruby
@audio.pause
```

# FmrbAudio#play

play(String path) -> void

Play a song file

Plays an NSF. The tunes live in /usr/share/sounds/nsf.
```ruby
@audio.play("/usr/share/sounds/nsf/test.nsf")
```

# FmrbAudio#play_slot

play_slot(Integer slot_id) -> void

Play the song in a slot

```ruby
@audio.play_slot(0)
```

# FmrbAudio#play_wav

play_wav(String path) -> bool

Play a recorded sound (WAV)

16-bit PCM, mono, 8000 to 48000Hz, up to 2MB. It plays over the APU.
Only one at a time: calling again while one sounds replaces it.
Retro cannot play it and gets false back (true when it does play).

# FmrbAudio#resume

resume() -> void

Carry on from the pause

```ruby
@audio.resume
```

# FmrbAudio#stop

stop() -> void

Stop the song

```ruby
@audio.stop
```

# FmrbAudio#stop_wav

stop_wav() -> bool

Stop the WAV that is playing

```ruby
@audio.stop_wav
```
