# Object#attr_accessor

attr_accessor(*Symbol names) -> nil

Define a reader and a writer

Gives both a reader and a writer. Written inside the class.
```ruby
class Foo
  attr_accessor :x, :y
end
```

# Object#attr_reader

attr_reader(*Symbol names) -> nil

Define a reader

**Reader only.**
```ruby
attr_reader :id
```

# Object#block_given?

block_given?() -> bool

Whether a block was given

Check before you `yield`.
```ruby
yield(v) if block_given?
```

# Object#class

class() -> Class

Return object class

```ruby
obj.class.name
```

# Object#dup

dup() -> self

Duplicate object

**A shallow copy**: what is inside is shared, not copied.
```ruby
b = a.dup
```

# Object#exit

exit(?Integer status) -> nil

End the app

Ends the app; the window is tidied up for you.
```ruby
exit
```

# Object#extend

extend(*untyped modules) -> nil

Add a module to this object alone

Adds the module to that one object.
```ruby
obj.extend(Bar)
```

# Object#include

include(*untyped modules) -> nil

Mix a module in

**A bare constant is not found through the including class** in picoruby;
write `self.class::NAME`.
```ruby
class Foo
  include Bar
end
```

# Object#inspect

inspect() -> String

Return string representation for debugging

```ruby
p obj
```

# Object#is_a?

is_a?(untyped class_or_module) -> bool

Check if instance of specified class or module

**There is no `defined?` here**; use this, `const_defined?`, or a rescue.
```ruby
if v.is_a?(Integer)
```

# Object#loop

loop() { (nil value) -> untyped } -> nil

Repeat forever

**Do not spin inside an app**: the shell can no longer deliver input.
```ruby
loop do
  break if done?
end
```

# Object.methods

methods() -> Array[Symbol]

get object method list

For finding out what an object answers to.
```ruby
p obj.methods
```

# Object#nil?

nil?() -> bool

Check if nil

```ruby
return if v.nil?
```

# Object#===

===(untyped other) -> bool

Judge case equality

```ruby
case v
when Integer then n
end
```

# Object#<=>

<=>(untyped other) -> Integer

Comparison operator

0 for the same object, nil otherwise.
```ruby
a <=> b
```

# Object#==

==(untyped other) -> bool

Perform equality comparison

**By default it asks whether they are the same object.** Define it
yourself to compare contents.
```ruby
if a == b
```

# Object#!=

!=(untyped other) -> bool

Perform inequality comparison

```ruby
if a != b
```

# Object#private

private(*Symbol names) -> nil

Make what follows private

```ruby
private
def helper
end
```

# Object#public

public(*Symbol names) -> nil

Make what follows public

```ruby
public
```

# Object#raise

raise(?untyped exception, ?String message) -> bot

Raise an exception

**It ends the app if nothing catches it.** Wrap file work in a `rescue`.
```ruby
raise "bad path"
begin
  risky
rescue => e
  Log.info(e.message)
end
```

# Object#relinquish

relinquish() -> bool

Give other tasks a turn

Hands the turn to other tasks; drop it into a long calculation and the
screen keeps moving.
```ruby
i = 0
while i < 10000
  relinquish if i % 500 == 0
  i += 1
end
```

# Object#sleep

sleep(Integer | Float duration) -> Integer

Wait, in seconds

Waits in seconds.
```ruby
sleep 1
```

# Object#sleep_ms

sleep_ms(Integer milliseconds) -> Integer

Wait, in milliseconds

**Not for use inside an app**: outside `_spin` the tick does not advance
and it never returns. Wait with `Machine.delay_ms`.
```ruby
Machine.delay_ms(50)
```

# Object#sprintf

sprintf(String format, *untyped arguments) -> String

Format a string

For lining figures up.
```ruby
s = sprintf("%3d%%", n)
```

# Object#to_s

to_s() -> String

Return string representation

```ruby
obj.to_s
```
