# Range#each

each() { (untyped element) -> untyped } -> self

Execute block for each element in range

**A block call costs about 0.4ms**; rewrite a hot loop as `while`.
```ruby
(0..7).each do |i|
  draw(i)
end
```

# Range#exclude_end?

exclude_end?() -> bool

Check if end value is excluded

true when it was made with `...`.
```ruby
(0...3).exclude_end?  #=> true
```

# Range#first

first() -> untyped

Return start value of range

```ruby
(1..5).first  #=> 1
```

# Range#inspect

inspect() -> String

Return string representation for debugging

```ruby
p (1..5)
```

# Range#last

last() -> untyped

Return end value of range

**The end as written**, even for `...` -- not the last element.
```ruby
(1...5).last  #=> 5
```

# Range.new

new(untyped first, untyped last, ?bool exclude_end) -> Range

Make a Range

Normally written `1..5`.
```ruby
r = Range.new(1, 5)
```

# Range#===

===(untyped object) -> bool

Check if value is included in range

**The form `case` uses.**
```ruby
case n
when 0..9 then digit
end
```

# Range#==

==(untyped other) -> bool

Perform equality comparison

```ruby
if r == other
```

# Range#to_s

to_s() -> String

Return string representation

```ruby
(1..5).to_s
```
