# Symbol#===

===(untyped other) -> bool

Perform equality comparison (for case statements)

```ruby
case k
when :name then hit
end
```

# Symbol#<=>

<=>(Symbol | untyped other) -> Integer

Compare symbols

```ruby
a <=> b
```

# Symbol#==

==(untyped other) -> bool

Perform equality comparison

Two equal symbols are the same object, so this is cheap.
```ruby
if k == :name
```

